2026-09-28T09:59:49.1094822Z     gate clauses carrying NO operator (prose inside the gate — not parsed, not judged, V-B's M2 method): 47
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1095430Z   `when` predicates as authored:
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1097336Z     Chart-boxplot                answers = distribution AND categories >= 2 AND each category carries a five-number summary AND span.cols <= 8 — roles.json when: "distribution per category"; beats Chart-histogram (roles.json: "distribution, one variable") whenever the spread must be read PER CATEGORY; yields to it when variables = 1 and the bin shape is the claim.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1100754Z     Chart-bullet                 answers=comparison AND the reading is one measure against a target plus qualitative performance bands AND span.cols 4–6 — beats stat-card (60, "default — label · value · delta · period, no series") and kpi-tile (50, "a series exists to show") when the BENCHMARK, not the delta and not a series, is the point; yields to both when no target exists.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1104049Z     Chart-butterfly-h            answers=comparison AND series=2 mirrored outward from a shared centre gutter AND categories ≥ 6 — beats chart-bar (grouped) when the two series must read as OPPOSED directions rather than adjacent columns; yields to Chart-butterfly-v (36, "as above, wide panel") when the category axis is ordered left-to-right and span.cols ≥ 8.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1107470Z     Chart-butterfly-v            answers=comparison AND series=2 mirrored above/below ONE horizontal baseline AND the category axis is ordered left-to-right (time, rank) AND span.cols ≥ 8 — yields to Chart-butterfly-h (40, "exactly two series mirrored, categories ≥ 6") whenever the categories are unordered or the panel is narrower than 8 cols; both yield to chart-bar for an ordinary grouped comparison.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1110929Z     Chart-candlestick            answers = change-over-time AND shape = periods × OHLC (open · high · low · close per session) — roles.json when: "OHLC per period"; beats chart-line (roles.json: "change-over-time") only when all four price points per period are the claim; yields to chart-line whenever one measure's path is enough.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1114418Z     Chart-histogram              answers = distribution AND variables = 1 AND bins = contiguous (no inter-bar gap) AND baseline = 0 — roles.json when: "distribution, one variable"; beats Chart-boxplot (roles.json: "distribution per category") when the frequency shape of ONE variable is the claim; yields to Chart-boxplot when categories >= 2; the no-gap rule is not cosmetic — the FT gives the same reason: "keep the gaps between columns small to highlight the 'shape' of the data".
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1118384Z     Chart-scatter                answers=relationship AND both axes carry quantitative measures — the ONLY provider of relationship in the role, so it beats every sibling on the answers gate alone and needs no further test; yields to chart-combo (56) when the two measures share one x axis in different units instead of being plotted against each other. span.cols max 8 because a runtime fit is not baked (this meta's own responsive rule).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1123499Z     alert                        the message is IN FLOW (inside the page or form it refers to) AND it persists until resolved or dismissed AND it carries a status glyph and a title, never colour alone AND an error alert never auto-dismisses — CANON-ADJACENT — our own purpose already states the three-way rule: "Use Toast for transient confirmations and Banner for page-level persistent messages; use inline field validation (Input-fields) for single-control errors"; beats toast (proposed "transient, no answer required") whenever the reader must act; beats banner (proposed "the condition governs the whole page or session") whenever the message belongs to one form or section — Atlassian draws the identical line: "For messages with information affecting the whole site, use a banner"; yields to inline field validation for a single control.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1127557Z     app-shell-focused            primaryNavigation = absent AND breadcrumbs = absent AND search = absent AND exits = 1 AND job.count = 1 — the only frame defined by removal; beats every other shell (roles.json: all six carry navigation) whenever abandoning the task is the failure mode — authentication, a wizard, a passcode; yields to app-shell-top-nav the moment the user must be able to go somewhere else.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1131798Z     app-shell-top-nav            destinations <= 7 AND nav.levels <= 2 — the default for dashboards — the bento template composes it; beats app-shell-side-nav (roles.json when: "> 7 destinations or two nav levels") below those bounds and app-shell-nav-rail (when: "dense app, content cannot spare 248px") when the content can spare the column; yields to app-shell-multi-column (when: "list-and-detail job") and to app-shell-focused (when: "one job, no navigation (auth, wizard)") when the job has no navigation. Co-providers of page-frame are mutually exclusive by construction (roles.json §05: one-at-a-time facility), so no not-with is authored.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1136170Z     breadcrumbs                  shape = ancestor-path × links AND depth >= 2 — beats anchor-nav (roles.json when: "in-page, long document") when the trail is ancestry rather than in-page position; yields to navigations (when: "global — masthead / main-nav family") for global movement and to tabs (when: "local — peer views in one context") for peer views — it answers where-am-i, they answer where-can-i-go, so it complements rather than replaces them.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1139808Z     button                       emphasis in (primary, secondary, tertiary, quaternary) AND label = text AND actions <= 1 — the default of the role; yields to icon-button (roles.json when: "space is tight and the glyph is universal") when label = glyph, to split-button (when: "one main action plus a menu of related ones") when a menu hangs off the action, and to links (when: "the action is navigation inside running text") when the action is navigation in prose.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1142309Z     chart-bar                    answers = comparison AND axis.x = categorical — beats chart-line (roles.json when: "change-over-time") when the x-dimension is categorical rather than a time continuum, and beats chart-pie (when: "composition, no centre figure, ≤ 5 parts") when the parts do not sum to a whole; the stacked variant takes composition across categories, where it yields to chart-stacked-area (when: "composition over time") if the axis is time.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1144443Z     chart-combo                  answers=change-over-time AND series=2 AND units=different AND both read against ONE shared x (dv-line-006) — beats chart-line (88, "change-over-time") on the different-units test and on nothing else; yields to chart-line (multi-series) or chart-bar (grouped) for a same-unit pair, which this meta's own antiPattern forbids drawing as a combo.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1146567Z     chart-donut                  answers=composition AND parts sum to a whole AND total=printed as a centre figure AND span.cols ≤ 6 — beats chart-pie (48, "composition, no centre figure, ≤ 5 parts") whenever the total is worth printing, and beats it on nothing else; yields to chart-stacked-area (64, "composition over time") when the split MOVES. A ring does not stretch with its tile (ds-030), so it takes a half-width column and never a full-width row (s305-D9).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1149337Z     chart-line                   answers=change-over-time AND series 1–5 on ONE continuous time axis AND axes=present AND span.cols ≥ 6 AND units = same AND shape = time-series × 1–5-series — the role's default at this intent, and it beats every sibling whose own `when` adds a further condition; yields to chart-combo (56, "two measures in different units over one axis") when units differ, to Chart-candlestick (44, "OHLC per period") when all four price points per period are the claim, and to chart-sparkline (30, "inline scale, no axes") when span.cols < 6.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1151815Z     chart-pie                    answers=composition AND parts ≤ 5 AND total=not printed AND span.cols ≤ 6 — yields to chart-donut (80, "composition, a centre total is meaningful") whenever a centre total is wanted, which is the only thing separating the two; yields to chart-stacked-area (64) when the split moves over time. A ring does not stretch with its tile (ds-030), so it takes a half-width column and never a full-width row (s305-D9).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1153706Z     chart-sparkline              answers=change-over-time AND series=1 AND axes=absent AND span.cols ≤ 4 (inline, or a trend cell in a table) — yields to chart-line (88, "change-over-time") whenever the panel can carry axes, and is normally a complement of headline-metric rather than a chart-panel in its own right (ROLES-REVIEW §03).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1155456Z     chart-stacked-area           answers spans change-over-time AND composition AND cumulative bands share ONE total across the time axis — beats chart-donut (80, "composition, a centre total is meaningful") and chart-pie (48) when the split MOVES rather than being a snapshot; yields to chart-line (88, "change-over-time") when the total is not meaningful.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1157096Z     data-grid                    records >= 2 AND needs in (sort, filter, select, edit) — the record-list for rows the person works on as a set: it beats list-items (the role's default, s274-D6) whenever sorting, filtering, selecting or editing is required, and yields to list-items when needs = none.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1158481Z     dropdown                     options >= 5 AND interrupts = none — one choice from a list, made in place (s270-D1: "we use dropdowns for 5 and above"); beats modals whenever the choice does not need to stop the person.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1159830Z     filter-toolbar-bar           records >= 2 AND needs in (filter, sort) — one row of controls that drives the record-list and the panels beside it (edges.drivesConsumer, s268-D5; the wiring is the author's, s258-D1); it is placed only above the thing it drives, never on its own.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1161252Z     footer                       platform = app — every app page shell ends in the app footer, the body-level sibling after the main region and never inside the bento wall (the meta's own $finding-site-footer, #258: "the page shells should include the footer").
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1163268Z     headers                      level in (page, screen, section) AND platform = app AND lockup = none — yields to page-header-lockup (roles.json when: "page level, with actions or tabs") whenever actions or tabs ride the band; beats section-heading-lockup (when: "section level, above one board / table / panel") because the Header Section Titles type covers the section level app-side, and beats eyebrow (when: "a kicker alone is enough (rare; normally a part of the above)") whenever a title, not a kicker, is wanted.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1166276Z     icon-button                  the control performs an action AND space is tight OR the glyph is universal AND an accessible name is supplied AND the hit target is at least 44x44 AND a tooltip carries the label — CANON on the first half (roles.json: "space is tight and the glyph is universal"); beats button only where the glyph is unambiguous — our own meta: "Use a labelled Button when the action is not unambiguous from a glyph alone"; the tooltip is not optional company: Atlassian ("Use tooltips with icon buttons to display the button label") and Polaris ("Be provided for icon-only buttons") both make it a requirement, which our meta states only as an antiPattern.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1169634Z     input-fields                 entry = free text AND expected answer fits ONE line AND no fixed option list exists AND the value is not money, a date, a time or a secret — the default text-entry field; beats textarea (proposed "the answer may span multiple lines") whenever the answer is a name, a reference or a phone number; yields to amount-input when the value is money, to date-picker / time-picker when it is a date or time, to secure-entry when it is a one-time code or PIN, and to dropdown or combobox whenever the answer must come from a list at all (Carbon: free text there "is likely to result in an error").
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1172246Z     kpi-tile                     shape = one-measure × value-delta-and-series AND series != none — beats stat-card (roles.json when: "default — label · value · delta · period, no series") whenever a series exists to show; yields to Chart-bullet (when: "a target or performance band is the point, not the delta") when target != none, and to runway-bar (when: "the number is 'money vs what is already scheduled'") when the measure is money-vs-scheduled.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1174422Z     layout-utilities             content = arbitrary-blocks AND surface = none — the default of the role; beats cards (roles.json when: "a bordered surface per item") whenever the arrangement must paint nothing, and beats stats-band-lockup (when: "3–6 headline-metrics in a labelled row") whenever the blocks are not headline-metrics; yields to divider (when: "a rule alone") when a rule alone is the whole need.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1176476Z     legend                       series ≥ 2 AND label = text — a key is needed only where more than one series is drawn; a single-series chart names its series in the title (chart-sparkline's rule). Placed on its own only when the charts it keys are more than one (small multiples, a comparison row); a lone chart carries its legend inside its own figure, which is what every registered chart type already does.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1178924Z     limits-meter                 INHERITS meter's gate, variant = allowance: the value is a cap being spent against AND full = BLOCKED, not done — a thin category alias of meter.meta.json (s210-D5); carries no independent when because writing spec into the alias is an explicit antiPattern on the parent — the reading is "how much of my limit is left", which is what roles.json already names.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1182770Z     list-items                   records >= 2 AND the records are the same kind, each read ACROSS its own row AND surface in (none, bordered-per-record) AND needs = none — surface ALONE decides the container (s274-D1): unbordered ⇒ simple-list (one line per record) or structured-list (aligned fields); a bordered surface drawn around EACH record ⇒ card-list. Actions are a ROW property, allowed in any of the three, so they decide nothing. No field count, row count or column count gates this (s274-D4): the comparison test decides — if a field must be read DOWN a column across records, it is a table, not a list. A list-level heading is OPTIONAL on all three containers (s274-D5); a per-card title is a ROW field, distinct from the list heading. Beats table (roles.json when: "default, read-mostly") and data-grid (when: "sort / filter / select / edit-in-place is required") whenever each record is read across its own row; yields to timeline (when: "time is the structure, records have happened") and to tree (when: "records nest").
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1186274Z     modals                       interrupts = required — the person must stop: confirm a consequential action, or finish a task that cannot share the screen; yields to split-button when interrupts = none AND actions >= 2 (one main action with a few related ones beside it), and to dropdown when interrupts = none AND options >= 5 (one choice from a list, made in place, s270-D1).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1188636Z     navigations                  shape = destination-set × links AND scope = global — the default of the role; beats breadcrumbs (roles.json when: "ancestry, depth ≥ 2") and tabs (when: "local — peer views in one context") because those are ancestry and local peers, not the global set; yields to sidebar-nav (when: "global, desktop, persistent column (pairs with app-shell-side-nav)") when the page-frame is app-shell-side-nav, and to tab-bar (when: "mobile bottom, 3–5 destinations") on mobile.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1191862Z     popover                      the content is STRUCTURED and FOCUSABLE AND it opens on CLICK from a labelled trigger AND it does not scroll AND it is non-modal (no focus trap, no aria-modal) AND only one is open — CANON-ADJACENT — our purpose already carries the three-way rule: "If the user can act inside it, it is a Popover; if it is a sentence of help text, it is a Tooltip; if it must interrupt, it is a Modal"; Atlassian states both halves independently ("For interactive overlays, use the modal dialog component" / "For non-essential, non-interactive messages, use the tooltip component"); yields to drawer or modals once the content scrolls (our antiPatterns[2], Atlassian: "Don't make popups that scroll", Carbon: past four columns wide use a modal).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1195291Z     runway-bar                   answers = one-number AND shape = one-measure × committed-vs-balance-split AND verdict != none — beats stat-card (60, "default — label · value · delta · period, no series") and kpi-tile (50, "a series exists to show") when the reading is "money vs what is already scheduled" and the takeaway is a VERDICT WITH A DATE rather than a delta or a trend; yields to stat-card when there is nothing committed to net off, to kpi-tile when a series is the claim, and to Chart-bullet (40, "a target or performance band is the point, not the delta") when a target band, not a coverage date, is the benchmark.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1197384Z     split-button                 actions >= 2 AND interrupts = none — one main action plus a menu of related ones, offered in place (button's own `when` already hands this case here); beats modals whenever the related actions can be offered without stopping the person.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1199260Z     stat-card                    shape = one-measure × value-and-delta AND series = none AND delta != none — the default of the role; beats kpi-tile (roles.json when: "a series exists to show (s247-D3 / DP-08: no series ⇒ not a KPI tile)") exactly when no series exists, and beats Chart-bullet (when: "a target or performance band is the point, not the delta") when the delta, not a band, is the claim.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1201221Z     status-indicator             shape = one-state × dot-and-label AND span.cols <= 4 — the default of the role; beats summary (roles.json when: "n × count as a key/value list, 6–12 cols") whenever exactly one state is read; yields to badge (when: "inline, attached to another element, count only") when the dot is attached to another element rather than standing alone.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1203295Z     summary                      shape = rows × name-value-pairs AND rows >= 2 AND span.cols >= 6 — beats status-indicator (roles.json when: "one state, one dot + label, 2–4 cols") whenever more than one row must be read at once; yields to meter (when: "the threshold is a cap being spent against (limits-meter reading)") when threshold = cap-spent-against, and to badge (when: "inline, attached to another element, count only") when the reading is inline.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1205411Z     template-confirmation        position = end of an instruction AND order = message, then FACTS, then actions, then what-happens-next AND a reference is shown if one exists — beats the Confirmation component (roles.json feedback role) because a confirmation PAGE is also the RECEIPT — that reordering is the template's whole contribution; ends a flow that template-wizard began.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1207527Z     template-dashboard-bento     the question is 'how are things, and what needs me?' AND layout.grammar = bento — the dashboard frame when the designer's answer to 'dashboard bento — is that right?' is yes (s230-D1 beat 2); its tiles are themselves bentos (s217-D2, s217-D3). A composer borrows its grammar ($bentoGrammar) and chooses every module from the graph; it yields to template-dashboard when layout.grammar = grid.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1209631Z     template-error               cause in (404, 500) AND RAG colour = unbound AND no support semantics invented AND one page serves ALL unexpected failures — beats template-empty (proposed "the query succeeded and returned nothing") because here the page could not be produced at all; beats an inline Alert (slice A) because the failure is the PAGE, not a field.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1211457Z     template-wizard              steps >= 2 AND order is enforced AND next is gated AND a review step precedes the end AND the end is a receipt — beats template-create-edit (proposed "one page, no enforced order") on order; composes app-shell-focused (roles.json when: "one job, no navigation (auth, wizard)") and borrows the step mechanism whole from Stepper.
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1214079Z     textarea                     entry = free text AND the answer may run to more than one line AND there is no fixed option list AND a length limit is shown only where a real limit exists — beats input-fields (proposed "the answer fits one line") the moment a sentence is expected rather than a value — notes to approvers, a reason for payment, a secure message body; yields to input-fields for anything shorter (GOV.UK, verbatim: "enter shorter answers no longer than a single line, such as a phone number"); the counter is added only when a limit genuinely exists (GOV.UK: "Only use the character count component when there is a good reason for limiting").
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1217044Z     timeline                     records >= 2 AND time IS the structure AND every record has ALREADY HAPPENED AND entries are not buttons AND order is newest-first with date headings — roles.json when: "time is the structure, records have happened"; beats list-items when the date rail is the reading rather than a sort order; yields to list-items inside a date group the moment entries must open (our AP1), and never borrows Progress-tracker's aria-current because there is no current step (our AP0).
2026-09-28T09:59:49.1219529Z     view-options                 NEVER — superseded 2026-07-24; the view switch is Segmented-control — carries no selection criterion because it is not a choice any composer should make: filter-toolbar-bar's AP1 already says "Consuming View-options instead of Segmented-control for the view switch — View-options was superseded"; the honest `when` here is a redirect, not a predicate.
